<title>USA: Three workers killed in airport garage collapse.</title>
<headline>Three workers killed in airport garage collapse.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three workers were killed Thursday  when a steel framework collapsed during construction of a $140 million  parking garage expansion at Portland International Airport, officials  said.</p>
<p>Part of a steel skeleton five stories high tilted and crashed to the  ground, eyewitnesses said.</p>
<p>Three construction workers who were on top of the steel structure  were killed, airport spokesman Daryl Buttice said.</p>
<p>The cause of the accident was unknown. Investigators were on the scene.</p>
</text>
